{"text":"Codex: I4 — land the three corpora and input-contract freeze.","body":{"conditions":"Start only after I3 lands. Implement section 2.8 corpora A/B/C and the input-contract freeze in the adopted design. Corpus A runs the immutable upstream module's own tests: go test -count=1 -json -run '^TestConformanceCorpus(ProjectionCases)?$' github.com/generalbusiness-ai/tailapps/jsonataddl. Verify exact v0.1.1 module sums and dependency pins, clear bypass variables, disable workspace/replaces, forbid -update-corpus, and require explicit passing events for BOTH TestConformanceCorpus and TestConformanceCorpusProjectionCases and their manifest cases. Zero matching tests is failure. No exported runner API or copied runner/corpus is needed. Corpus B compares existing deterministic cases with live jsonata-js 2.0.6 and proves ambient/order-dependent forms compile-refuse. Corpus C compares the reviewed old spike runtime and new host over the same sealed fixture log: ordered decisions including absences, ordered facts, and final stock/reservations rows. Only runtime/source identity and program names may be excluded; no third exclusion. Freeze complete EvaluationInput (empty meta/rows objects), every event scalar, empty and ordered two-element rests_on without sorting/deduplication, and exact-bound numeric payload decoding. Run all corpora twice at the exact head and show a deliberately wrong upsert fails C. Keep oracle evidence isolated and reproducible; raise a repair request if retaining its dependency prevents I9. No binding migration or production activation.\n\nGoverning design: /Users/hughpyle/play/gitseq/notes/2026-09-04-tailapps-jsonataddl-adoption.md at Gitseq commit 860ee61a07aa753dcbc2d50e74da2b7b6547625b, sections 2 and 5, adopted by Hugh in the Gitseq room and bridged here by 8812cc62. Inspect that foreign authority; this bridge does not invent local ratification. Module is github.com/generalbusiness-ai/tailapps/jsonataddl v0.1.1, Sum h1:rzas2PYo0x3n9K6lLo42l3ZLyN16VwHpUjDMtRFZaRg=, GoModSum h1:fpGrE/1ODSULhyxThhr3TL4JtpfcX3PdA4kJBnKWJRY=. JSONata must remain v0.0.0-20250709164031-599f35f32e5f and ncruces/go-sqlite3 v0.35.3; any drift requires version-skew analysis and corpus evidence before proceeding. No production-log interpretation until deterministic step and allocation bounds exist; preserve and visibly enforce the fixture-only limitation. Do not treat wall-clock timeout as a semantic bound. No Tailapps root dependency or copied compiler/evaluator. Work only in this repository, in a new request/\u003cslug\u003e branch/worktree from current refs/heads/main (remote measured at filing: 7cfdc271503f490a4f80b533bc64ec27b3ce9a49; root checkout is behind). Publish exact artifacts, update affected architecture documentation in the same head, run meaningful formatting, vet, tests, focused race, build, dependency/license/security and clean-tree checks, obtain independent Architecture/Security/Simplification review (planner or Claude), ratify, seal the exact approved merge, push, verify available CI and clean your worktree/branch safely. No rm -f or rm -rf. A reporting artifact alone does not satisfy delivery. Planner owns repair requests and authority coordination; address missing prerequisites to planner. Establish suitable CI as a bounded child if required; do not silently claim an absent check passed. Record each landed head and receipt for the Gitseq coordination report.","to":"826c05d4fd56efee52cb270debdccd04322835c8dd312ec29c01dc33a9ebe003"},"expectation":{"request":"git:sha1:5abaa0f151cd76dcf02a7bd669358ce94b67f4a6#git:sha1:03a94fc577c8d6d5dc9abfd9b6fb8993d948459e","retirement":"git:sha1:5abaa0f151cd76dcf02a7bd669358ce94b67f4a6#git:sha1:1d7c3c70792c1d95c420e38b0e9e0ae65e645648","promise":"absent","completion":"absent"}}